# hw/silence: from its answer on, the driver sends nothing to the board for seconds (no heartbeat, no setpoint, no
# blade frame), drops what it is asked meanwhile and keeps publishing what it reads. Then it latches the emergency
# (HIGH_LEVEL), sends the blade off and three stops, and goes on as before. Offered where hw/capabilities has
# silence_max_s > 0, and only while a step of the setup program runs; the setup program measures with it how the board
# stops without its host.
float32 seconds
# The blade may be on or turning: the driver goes silent all the same, and the board has to stop the blade without
# its host. Without it the driver refuses with BLADE.
bool blade
---
bool success
string message
# Why it was refused, empty otherwise: READ_ONLY, OUT_OF_RANGE (seconds not in 0.2 to silence_max_s), NO_SETUP (no
# active setup/motion within the last second), CHARGING (on the charging contacts), BLADE (blade on or still turning
# without blade), BUSY (already silent).
string code
